course: dictionary
lesson: 4995
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indonesian can be a describing word, a name for a person, or the name of a language. Context tells you which one. In «The Komodo dragon ... lives on a few Indonesian islands», Indonesian describes the islands, so it means from Indonesia.
explain: Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence. If it is describing a thing, like «an Indonesian fish market» in «a second kind was found at an Indonesian fish market in 1997», it means from or about Indonesia. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: If the word is about speaking or learning, as in «speak Indonesian», it means the language. If it names a person, as in «Indonesians», it means people from Indonesia. Indonesia is a large country in Southeast Asia made of thousands of islands.
fact: Indonesia is a large country in Southeast Asia made of thousands of islands.
fact: Indonesian can be an adjective, a noun for a person, or the name of a language.
fact: An Indonesian is a person from Indonesia; the national language is called Bahasa Indonesia.
fact: The Komodo dragon, up to 3 metres long, is the biggest lizard, and it lives on a few Indonesian islands.
fact: In Indonesian, doubling a noun makes it plural: «buku» means book, and «buku-buku» means books.
exercise: In «it lives on a few Indonesian islands», what does Indonesian describe? | the lizard | *the islands | the deer it hunts
exercise: Mia says, «Indonesians cook amazing food.» What does Indonesians mean here? | the Indonesian language | *people from Indonesia | the islands of Indonesia | a kind of fish
exercise: Ben says, «I can speak Indonesian.» What does Indonesian mean here? | an island | people from Indonesia | *the language | a volcano
test: In «a second kind was found at an Indonesian fish market in 1997», what does Indonesian describe? | the coelacanth's home in South Africa | *the fish market | the year 1997 | the scientists
test: In Indonesian, what is the plural of «rumah» (house)? | house-house | rumah | rumahs | *rumah-rumah
exam: Which sentence uses Indonesian as a noun for a person? | The Komodo dragon lives on Indonesian islands. | The Indonesian fish market was busy. | *Two Indonesians met us at the airport. | She speaks Indonesian at school.
